                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Draft Clause for Treaty of Commerce and Navigation
                        with Siam</hi></head>
                <p>The United States of America recognizes that the principle of national autonomy
                    should apply to the Kingdom of Siam in all that pertains to the rates of duty on
                    importations and exportations of merchandise, drawbacks, and transit and other
                    inland taxes; and subject to the guarantees of the present treaty to equality of
                    treatment with other nations in these respects the United States of America
                    agrees to assent to increases by Siam in tariff rates higher than those
                    established by existing treaties, on condition, however, that all other nations
                    entitled to claim special tariff treatment in Siam assent to such increases
                    freely and without the requirement of any compensatory benefit or privilege.</p>
            </div>
